    "stmbench/vista/__main__.py"
   ],
   "why": "cap OMP/BLAS threads at 4 per episode process (performance only): oversubscription starved the sim's synchronous scan render past MAST's 5 s timeout (seed0 img P1: every StartScan timed out)",
   "applies_from": "episodes started after the patch"
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-10-09 21:50",
   "from_digest": "3632f3eb9e95",
   "to_digest": "e847e3f3cd8c",
   "files": [
    "stmbench/vista/actions.py",
    "stmbench/vista/host.py"
   ],
   "why": "vigil-text arm: spectra observed as a numeric table (MAST's skills returned curve numbers; VIGIL never saw curves); act description says so. Image arms unchanged.",
   "applies_from": "episodes started after the patch; all vigil-text episodes of seeds 0 and 1 ran before it and are rerun"
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-10-09 23:42",
   "from_digest": "e847e3f3cd8c",
   "to_digest": "675308f7ddfc",
   "files": [
    "stmbench/vista/claude_runner.py"
   ],
   "why": "billing: RunnerConfig.auth='subscription' (default) drops ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN from the claude child env and refuses a session whose init reports an API key source. Before this, MAST's runtime host exported the repo's Anthropic key and every VISTA episode billed it (~$52) until its balance ran out at ~23:00.",
   "applies_from": "episodes started after the patch (model, prompts and tools unchanged)"
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-10-10 01:43",
   "from_digest": "675308f7ddfc",
   "to_digest": "42aa96a42fb2",
   "files": [
    "stmbench/harness/runtime_host.py",
    "stmbench/vista/episode.py"
   ],
   "why": "simulator reply timeout: RuntimeHost(nanonis_timeout_s=...) opt-in; VISTA episodes use 60 s because stmsim renders a whole frame inside Scan_Action (2-15 s for large Au(111) frames) and MAST's 5 s default dropped the connections (P1 episodes with 3-123 connection losses).",
   "applies_from": "episodes started after the patch; the three P1 episodes with connection losses are rerun"
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-10-10 02:38",
   "from_digest": "42aa96a42fb2",
